  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRIVATE-SECTOR SUPPORT FOR THE DELIVERY OF KENYA S BLACK RHINO ACTION PLAN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT A CONSERVATION EFFORT IN OL JOGI CONSERVANCY, BORANA CONSERVANCY, LEWA WILDLIFE CONSERVANCY, AND ON THE ASSOCIATION OF PRIVATE AND COMMUNITY LAND RHINO SANCTUARIES IN KENYA BY STRENGTHENING RHINOCEROS PROTECTION, BIOLOGICAL MONITORING, AND COORDINATION. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE THE EASTERN BLACK RHINOCEROS BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF RHINOCEROS POACHING, THE NEED FOR BIOLOGICAL MANAGEMENT FOR RHINOCEROS, AND THE NEW THREATS TO THE CONSERVANCIES INCOME GENERATION DUE TO THE LOSS OF REVENUE FROM TOURISM AND OTHER GLOBAL ECONOMIC FACTORS BECAUSE OF COVID-19. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) INCREASING RHINOCEROS PROTECTION (2) MONITORING AND MANAGEMENT OF RHINOCEROS POPULATIONS IN ORDER TO OPTIMIZE GROWTH, EXPAND THEIR RANGE, AND MAINTAIN GENETIC DIVERSITY AND (3) COORDINATING AND COLLABORATING ON EFFECTIVE PROJECT MANAGEMENT WITH PRIVATE AND COMMUNITY LAND CONSERVANCIES AS A CONTRIBUTION TO THE KENYA BLACK RHINO ACTION PLAN 2022-2026.</narrative>
  </description>
